<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:07:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>37 die in Nigerian custody: Reports blame overcrowding, government disputes claim</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/37-die-in-nigerian-custody-reports-blame-overcrowding-government-disputes-claim</link><description>
Authorities in north-central Nigeria are investigating the deaths of 37 people while they were in custody for illegal mining. Officials say the detainees died at a detention facility in Niger state, with the Nigerian Security and Civil Defence Corps pointing to a possible disease outbreak. However, some reports suggest overcrowding and poor ventilation may have contributed to the deaths. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent Sam Olukoya.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65545b5a-b41b-11f1-a160-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-214253-214509-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65545b5a-b41b-11f1-a160-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-214253-214509-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ad88ae2-b41b-11f1-b1e4-1314eca9ae5c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:26:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukrainian children learn ancient warrior skills amid modern war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-children-learn-ancient-warrior-skills-amid-modern-war</link><description>
Ukrainian children are learning the skills of 17th-century Cossack warriors – the communities that played a central role in Ukraine history, known for their military skills and horsemanship. But for these students, it is more than a history lesson. It is a chance to escape the reality of growing up during war. Story by Charlotte Lam.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/218ca4dc-b41a-11f1-899b-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-121041-121212-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/218ca4dc-b41a-11f1-899b-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-121041-121212-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">273a82c8-b41a-11f1-9be6-4f06459a85cc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:21:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New France football boss Zidane names first squad</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/new-france-football-boss-zidane-names-first-squad</link><description>
Football legend Zinedine Zidane says that Kylian Mbappe will be his France captain. Zidane named his first squad since being appointed head coach of France's national football team. His first matches in charge will be against Turkey and Belgium. Details by Nick Rushworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b49eac1c-b419-11f1-ad21-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-082227-082406-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b49eac1c-b419-11f1-ad21-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-082227-082406-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9ee6c70-b419-11f1-b188-7da21c979168</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:20:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Suspected alcohol poisoning in Nigeria's Ondo State kills at least 49 people</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/suspected-alcohol-poisoning-in-nigeria-s-ondo-state-kills-at-least-49-people</link><description>
In Nigeria's Ondo state, at least 49 people have died and 100 others injured after drinking alcohol suspected to contain methanol. Local authorities say 'Monkey Shoulder', a locally brewed herbal drink with high alcohol content is believed to have been the source of the poisoning, but investigations are still ongoing. State police have announced the arrest of 15 people in connection with the incident. Story by Clemence Waller.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ceee4ea-b415-11f1-8462-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-081623-081755-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ceee4ea-b415-11f1-8462-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-081623-081755-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62cd3416-b415-11f1-9ce2-757b5e461cca</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:19:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Did Trump really obtain 'permanent control' over Greenland?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland</link><description>
Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen has described a deal for the US to develop a significant military presence on Greenland, as 'a good agreement'. US President Donald Trump announced the deal on Friday, after he spent months seeking to acquire Greenland, citing threats from Russia and China, and even raised the possibility of military action. Story by Charlotte Hughes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d16ac90-b41a-11f1-a12f-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T000307Z-1543419715-RC2WLNA3UJU3-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-MIGRATION-VISA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d16ac90-b41a-11f1-a12f-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T000307Z-1543419715-RC2WLNA3UJU3-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-MIGRATION-VISA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a7c6e06-b414-11f1-8de3-fb275c31dbd8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:07:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump claims son repaid Russian oligarch who funded wedding festivities</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son had repaid a Kremlin-linked Russian businessman who funded two days of lavish wedding celebrations in the Bahamas, after the gift raised questions over foreign influence and ethics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bf90a56-b411-11f1-a68f-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T215141Z-974609741-RC2MHNAMNM5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-SON-WEDDING.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bf90a56-b411-11f1-a68f-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T215141Z-974609741-RC2MHNAMNM5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-SON-WEDDING.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e34518c-b413-11f1-9b21-7bccead38d01</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:26:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bf90a56-b411-11f1-a68f-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T215141Z-974609741-RC2MHNAMNM5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-SON-WEDDING.jpg">© Kylie Cooper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany cuts energy tax to lower petrol prices as Merz faces state key elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices</link><description>
Germany will cut taxes on gasoline and diesel by about 17 cents a litre from October, the government said Friday. The move comes ahead of state elections in the capital Berlin and the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania where Chancellor Friedrich Merz's conservative Christian Democrats are expected to be soundly defeated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0960e532-b409-11f1-ae11-9f86e9d8151e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:05:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg">© Angelika Warmuth, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Japan under pressure amid accommodation woes as Asian Games kick off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off</link><description>
It’s the world's biggest sporting event, held every four years – the 20th edition of Asian games is starting in Japan. Organisers came under pressure even before competition began… as thousands more athletes and officials registered to take part than initially expected. Story by Charlotte Lam.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c89f7228-b40f-11f1-b632-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-092208-092418-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c89f7228-b40f-11f1-b632-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-092208-092418-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdd29f86-b40f-11f1-8e30-357cf33607c2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:02:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ebola outbreak reaches new areas in Democratic Republic of Congo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ebola-outbreak-reaches-new-areas-in-democratic-republic-of-congo</link><description>
In the Democratic Republic of Congo, the government claims that the Ebola outbreak has changed course, with cases trending downwards in hotspots. But that interpretation is being met with pushback from experts and health responders, who say the outbreak remains as bad as ever. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent Emmet Livingstone.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/869cc4c2-b40d-11f1-88bb-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-092014-092142-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/869cc4c2-b40d-11f1-88bb-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-092014-092142-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c62d3c4-b40d-11f1-9cd8-8bb2ea9db659</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:59:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain's police launch operation to clear migrants off Ceuta beach</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach</link><description>
Police on Friday moved hundreds of migrants from the beaches of Ceuta to a temporary camp in the Spanish enclave's port area. The police operation takes place weeks after a record influx of people into Spain's North African tiny territory. During the transfer, the police struggled to contain crowds jostling to get a place at the new tented site. The policing takes place with the issue of migration centre stage in Spain's political debate. Details by Nicholas Rushworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73cc7560-b410-11f1-b9a7-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T111329Z-520083964-RC2JLNA3KNDI-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73cc7560-b410-11f1-b9a7-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T111329Z-520083964-RC2JLNA3KNDI-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b26b6802-b40c-11f1-b11d-c1e3642d6b2e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:57:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France’s Macron warns of Russian ‘hybrid’ attacks, seeks to step up energy defence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence</link><description>
Just months before France's presidential election, rising fuel costs due to the wars in Iran and Ukraine have pushed the nation to the verge of crisis. In an attempt to address public anger and energy threats, French President Emmanuel Macron gathered the nation's major party presidential candidates at the presidential palace. But the main takeaway from this meeting was perhaps Macron's warning about Russian "hybrid attacks"... what exactly does he mean and how serious is the threat? Details and analysis by Richard Werly, France and Europe correspondent for Blick.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0eb8d6d6-b40c-11f1-8370-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-090800-091732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0eb8d6d6-b40c-11f1-8370-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-090800-091732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">147ffc84-b40c-11f1-952d-eb991228bdb8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:52:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground</link><description>
Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4e9a5ae-b407-11f1-b2e8-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T131305Z-414222399-RC2OLNAJ0IX0-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3451f910-b405-11f1-9cb8-2d26d5c2c2ec</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:57:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Princess Diana's iconic 'revenge dress' goes to auction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/princess-diana-s-iconic-revenge-dress-goes-to-auction</link><description>
As the worldwide release of Diana Spencer’s brother’s book prompts a reaction from King Charles and the British Crown, another piece of Diana's legacy is making headlines – the iconic little black dress, worn by the then Princess of Wales, is going under the hammer. Better known as the "Revenge Dress", it would go on to inspire generations of women.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0160137e-b406-11f1-8f9a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100959-101205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0160137e-b406-11f1-8f9a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100959-101205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07125c64-b406-11f1-a249-b17150f714a3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:57:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump bans three media outlets from the White House, accusing them of spreading 'fake news'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news</link><description>
Donald Trump announced Friday he is banning CNN, MS NOW and Politico from the White House, accusing all three outlets of spreading 'fake news'. The move is almost certain to face legal challenges, and has been denounced by press freedom advocates. The US president's relationship with media outlets has long been fraught, as Charlotte Hughes explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7937e158-b404-11f1-949a-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100431-100620-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7937e158-b404-11f1-949a-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100431-100620-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e86af7c-b404-11f1-9970-f7a0c9fbd459</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:53:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Denmark reach deal on Greenland, Trump claims 'permanent control' over island</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-deal-on-greenland-trump-claims-permanent-control-over-island</link><description>
Not so long ago, inhabitants of Greenland feared that the US was preparing to invade, after US President Donald Trump repeatedly claimed the US wanted to control the Arctic territory. But Trump now says he has struck a deal with Denmark to give Washington "permanent control" over Greenland's security, while ensuring the territory remains firmly in the hands of Denmark. Denmark and Greenland have both hailed the deal, but its exact terms remain unclear. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Washington, Fraser Jackson.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2eeb8a66-b407-11f1-894d-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T213943Z-633036686-RC2OFNA6L8V8-RTRMADP-3-USA-DENMARK-GREENLAND-TALKS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2eeb8a66-b407-11f1-894d-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T213943Z-633036686-RC2OFNA6L8V8-RTRMADP-3-USA-DENMARK-GREENLAND-TALKS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8582cd4-b403-11f1-a180-1ba83d71ed50</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:48:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Scientists discover first new wild cat in more than 100 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years</link><description>
Scientists have identified a previously unknown species of wild cat living at a wildlife sanctuary in Bolivia. The tiny, spotted feline had lived at the sanctuary for years before genetic analysis revealed it as the first new living wild cat species identified in more than a century.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ec2ec0-b39a-11f1-9230-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154146Z-238128909-RC2KANAC4Y4W-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-CAT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ec2ec0-b39a-11f1-9230-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154146Z-238128909-RC2KANAC4Y4W-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-CAT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01f0463e-b405-11f1-a2ea-c7baa8e04b02</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:44:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ec2ec0-b39a-11f1-9230-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154146Z-238128909-RC2KANAC4Y4W-RTRMADP-3-SCIENCE-CAT.jpg">© Fernando Faciole, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France: Zinédine Zidane brings a breath of fresh air to Les Bleus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260919-france-zin%C3%A9dine-zidane-brings-a-breath-of-fresh-air-to-les-bleus</link><description>
For his first squad announcement on Friday, new France boss Zinédine Zidane made it clear he intends to break with Didier Deschamps. Five new faces, an attacking philosophy ... Ahead of his first games in charge in the Nations League, “ZZ” is bringing a breath of fresh air to Les Bleus.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d16118ce-b3da-11f1-8657-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8Q33UR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d16118ce-b3da-11f1-8657-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8Q33UR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">40f3bda4-b3db-11f1-9fc5-a582be557f41</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:10:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Cuba hit with another nationwide blackout amid US fuel blockade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness</link><description>
Cuba suffered a total blackout after the collapse of its electrical grid on Friday. The blackout is the latest of at least six partial or total grid collapses since the beginning of this year, as the island grapples with an ongoing US fuel blockade. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2b2e658-b3f1-11f1-86c9-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T022744Z-1614561925-RC2ZLNANNZ5Y-RTRMADP-3-CUBA-CRISIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2b2e658-b3f1-11f1-86c9-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T022744Z-1614561925-RC2ZLNANNZ5Y-RTRMADP-3-CUBA-CRISIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cda15226-b3f3-11f1-805c-f1b92cace8c8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 06:31:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2b2e658-b3f1-11f1-86c9-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T022744Z-1614561925-RC2ZLNANNZ5Y-RTRMADP-3-CUBA-CRISIS.jpg">© Ricardo Arduengo, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia reports cyberattacks as parliamentary vote enters second day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-ukraine-live-russian-strike-on-apartment-building-in-ukraine-s-sumy-kills-at-least-two</link><description>
Russia said Saturday that its electronic voting system in Moscow had come under “powerful” cyberattacks overnight, as parliamentary elections entered their second day. Russian President Vladimir Putin on Friday accused Ukraine of seeking to “hinder” the vote, a claim Kyiv has not publicly addressed. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.
